    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n25902" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Largus</span></b> , i, m., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a Roman surname</i>,
			esp. in the gens Scribonia, <i><span class="en">Cic. Fam. 6, 8, 1</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. de
				Or. 2, 59, 240</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">P. Largus Caecina,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Tac.
					A. 11, 33</span></i>
			.—Hence, </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Largĭānus</span></b> ,
				a, um, <i>adj., of</i> or <i>belonging to a Largus, Largian</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">senatusconsultum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Just. Inst. 3, 7 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			</div>
